course: dictionary
lesson: 3387
title: Words that grow: expand
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To expand means to become bigger, or to make something bigger. A balloon expands when you blow air into it. Its shape gets larger because the air inside takes up more room.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «The universe is expanding, which means it is getting bigger over time.» The words getting bigger tell you that expanding means growing larger.
explain: Expand can also mean to say or write more about an idea. When a teacher asks you to expand on your answer, she wants more detail, not a longer copy of the question.
explain: In maths, «expanded form» means writing a number as the sum of its place values. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: Expand means to become bigger, or to make something bigger.
fact: To «expand on» an idea means to say or write more about it.
fact: In maths, «expanded form» writes a number as the sum of its place values: 352 = 300 + 50 + 2.
fact: Most materials expand when heated and contract, which means they get smaller, when cooled.
fact: Water is unusual because it expands when it freezes, which can burst pipes.
exercise: «A balloon expands when you blow air into it.» What does expands mean here? | Turns a new colour | Gets smaller | Floats away | *Gets bigger
exercise: Your teacher says, «Can you expand on your answer?» What does she want? | Stop talking | Less writing, just one word | Copy the question out | *Say or write more about your idea
exercise: Write 352 in expanded form. | *300 + 50 + 2 | 35 + 2 | 352 + 0 | 3 + 5 + 2
test: «Most materials contract when they are cooled.» What does contract mean here? | Melt into liquid | *Get smaller | Shine brightly | Get bigger
test: Which sentence uses expand to mean make something grow and cover more? | *The company wants to expand into new towns. | The cat slept all day. | He ran to the shop. | The bell rang at noon.
exam: Why does ice float? | *Water expands when it freezes, so ice is lighter than the same amount of water | Ice is made of air | Ice is heavier than water | Water shrinks when it freezes
